          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "areaCm2",
          "label": "Sheet Area",
          "formula": "(inputs.sizeA * inputs.sizeB) / 100",
          "unit": "cm²",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "areaM2",
          "label": "Sheet Area",
          "formula": "(inputs.sizeA * inputs.sizeB) / 1000000",
          "unit": "m²",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## About ISO A-Series Sheet Sizes\n\nThe ISO A0 sheet size is defined as having an area of exactly one square meter (1 m²). Each subsequent size in the series is derived by dividing the previous size in half:\n\n- An A0 sheet cut in half gives two A1 sheets\n- An A1 sheet cut in half gives two A2 sheets\n- And so on...\n\nThis creates a geometric progression where each size maintains the same aspect ratio (1:√2) while halving the area."
    }
  ]
